{
    "background_story": "Zachariah was a mystic poet who spent his life chasing the empyrean, the highest realm of heaven. He believed that the key to unlocking the secrets of the universe lay in the celestial bodies that twinkled above. As a young man, Zachariah would often sneak out of his village at night to gaze up at the stars, feeling the infinite vastness of the cosmos calling to him. His poetry became a reflection of his quest for the divine, with verses that soared on the wings of imagination. As his fame grew, so did his obsession with the empyrean. Zachariah spent years studying ancient texts and practicing ascetic rituals, seeking to transcend the mundane and reach the sublime. His work became a testament to the human spirit's capacity for striving towards the infinite and the eternal.",
